🧹 Maintenance & Troubleshooting CommandsCheck 
        
Application Logs:
Bash
    docker compose logs -f backend-service
Specific  docker container log:    docker logs -f mcrm_postgres
Stop All Running Services:
Bash
    docker compose --profile local-db down

Reset Local Database (Wipe Data & Re-seed):
Bash
    docker compose --profile local-db down -v
    docker compose --profile local-db up --build -d
DB login:
psql -U crm_admin -d mcrm  -- In Docker Desktop exec tab.
docker exec -it mcrm_postgres psql -U crm_admin -d mcrm  --CMD/PS1
mcrm=# SELECT * FROM Master_Product;
***Why You Need Dockerfiles (inside individula project)**
Docker Compose coordinates and runs your services, but it doesn't know how to package or run your code unless you provide instructions.

docker-compose.yml is the Manager: It defines network bridges, port mappings, volumes, environment variables, and how containers talk to each other.

Dockerfile is the Recipe: It lives inside each project folder (./backend and ./frontend). It tells Docker:

What base runtime to install (e.g., Node.js or Python, Nginx).

How to copy your code into the container.

Which dependencies to install (npm install or pip install).

How to build assets (e.g., compiling React TSX into static HTML/JS).

What exact command starts the app inside the container.

Without Dockerfiles, running docker compose up --build will fail because Docker cannot build the container images for backend-service and frontend-ui.